                <head>Count Bismarck to Baron Gerolt.</head>
                <p>After the news of the renunciation of the hereditary Prince of Hohenzollern had
                    been officially communicated to the French imperial government by the royal
                    Spanish government, the French ambassador at Ems demanded from his Majesty the
                    King authorization to telegraph to Paris that his Majesty the King would bind
                    himself for all future time not to give his assent in case the Hohenzollern
                    should return to their candidacy. His Majesty the King thereupon declined again
                    to receive the French ambassador, and replied to him, through his aide-de-camp,
                    that he had no further communication to make to him.</p>
            </div>
